+- `patches/dsh-settings-section-icon.patch`: proposed general-purpose harness change adding an optional `icon` registration option to list slots, so a `settings.section` page can contribute its own nav glyph instead of relying on the installed-shell patch.
+- `scripts/patch-dsh-settings-nav-icon.mjs` now derives the `*Medium` / `*16` glyph variant from the installed shell, verifies the chosen export against the served frontend bundle (a missing export blanks the settings page through the React #130 slot failure), replaces a stale insert left by an earlier DSH generation, and accepts an install root that contains the `@deepseek-ai/dsh` package.
+
+### Changed
+
+- The host resolves its Config seam by capability: `settings.register` for DSH 0.1.1-rc.2 through 0.1.5-rc.x, an exported volatile-root `Config` plus `settings.mutate` for 0.1.7-rc.1 and newer. The Adapter registers `configure({ auto: false })` so the harness does not also generate a generic form for its entry.
+- The client awaits `configForms` or `settingsScope` through a `ctx.inject` child instead of declaring either statically, so neither generation parks the plugin fiber waiting for a service that never mounts.
+- `package.json` drops the removed `@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-runtime` from `dsh.client.inject`, widens the settings peer with `^0.1.7-rc.2`, and dev-depends on `@deepseek-ai/schemastery` `^3.18.4` (the schema call is feature-detected so a 3.18.1 host still loads).
