+# DSH 0.1.7-rc.2 Config migration verification
+
+Date: 2026-10-14
+
+## Environment
+
+- DSH: `@deepseek-ai/dsh` `0.1.7-rc.2`, installed tree at `.dsh-migrate/dsh/dsh-0.1.7-rc.2`.
+- Harness source: `.dsh-migrate/harness` at tag `dsh-v0.1.7-rc.2`.
+- Profile: an isolated `$DSH_HOME=/tmp/dsh-smoke`, profile `rescue` created from the shipped `web` template, with this package added by `dsh plugin --profile rescue add <repo>` (the row composes as `- id: mcp`).
+- Client bundle: `pnpm build` output `lib/client.js`, served from the linked package.
+
+## Static and unit checks
+
+- `pnpm install` and `pnpm build`: passed.
+- `pnpm test`: 164 of 164 tests passed, including the new 0.1.7 `configForms` generation fake, the entry-Config scope tests, and the legacy 0.1.1/0.1.2/0.1.5 generation fakes.
+- `scripts/patch-dsh-settings-nav-icon.mjs` was exercised against a copy of the installed shell: it derived `IconLinkOutlineMedium`, inserted the branch after the `models` branch, refused a deliberately wrong `--icon IconLinkOutline16` with the React #130 warning, replaced a stale insert, and reverted byte-identically.
+
+## Runtime checks
+
+1. `node bin/dsh --profile rescue --dump-config` composed the row as `- id: mcp` / `name: '@auggieteo/dsh-mcp-adapter'`.
+2. `node bin/dsh --profile rescue --dump-config-schema` embedded the exported Config in the profile schema with `"x-cordis": {"volatile": true}` and the full `mcpServers` field set, proving the host half's Config schema reaches the loader on 0.1.7.
+3. `node bin/dsh --profile rescue --no-open --port 0` booted the web profile with no loader or plugin error.
+4. The served index carried the client row `{"id":"@auggieteo/dsh-mcp-adapter","inject":["@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-connection","@deepseek-ai/dsh-api-remotes","@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-ui-settings"],"immediately":true}` — without the removed `@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-runtime` — and the plugin's `client.js` combo in the application batch.
+5. A seeded `$DSH_HOME/settings.yaml` with an `mcp:` section was imported once into the profile patch (`profiles/rescue/cordis.patch.yml`) as the row's `config:`, including the non-server `skillInstall`, and `settings.yaml` was renamed to `settings.yaml.imported`. This is the check that fails if the row id is not `mcp` or if the Config root is not volatile.
+
+## Not covered
+
+- No browser session was driven, so the rendered Settings > MCP page, its form writes, and the OAuth sign-in flow were not exercised against 0.1.7.
+- The upstream `patches/dsh-settings-section-icon.patch` was applied to the harness checkout and reverse-checked, but the harness test suite could not run because that sparse checkout has no installed workspace dependencies.
+
+## Second pass (2026-10-14, review of the recorded migration)
+
+Re-ran the mechanical checks and added two focused checks that do not need the
+harness workspace to be installed:
+
+- `pnpm test`: 164 of 164 pass; `pnpm build`: clean. The emitted bundle carries
+  `id: "@auggieteo/dsh-mcp-adapter"` (equal to `package.json#name`, the
+  client-modules registration contract) and contains no `dsh-client-runtime`
+  reference. It awaits its two settings generations through separate
+  `ctx.inject(["configForms"])` and `ctx.inject(["settingsScope"])` children, so
+  neither can park the module.
+- Peer floor measured against the host's own checker: the installed 0.1.7-rc.2
+  tree resolves semver `7.8.5`, and
+  `semver.satisfies('0.1.7-rc.2', '^0.1.1-rc.2 || ^0.1.2-rc.1 || ^0.1.5-rc.1 || ^0.1.7-rc.2', { includePrerelease: true })`
+  is `true`, so `dsh plugin add` and startup accept the Adapter on this host.
+- `scripts/patch-dsh-settings-nav-icon.mjs` was exercised against a copy of the
+  real 0.1.7-rc.2 installed shell and primitives/frontend artifacts: it derived
+  `IconLinkOutlineMedium`, refused the removed `IconLinkOutline16` with the
+  React #130 warning (exit 1), was idempotent on a second run, replaced a stale
+  `IconLinkOutlineRegular` insert instead of stacking a second branch, and
+  reverted byte-identically.
+- `patches/dsh-settings-section-icon.patch` reverse-checks exactly against the
+  `dsh-v0.1.7-rc.2` working tree (`git apply --check --reverse`), and its
+  option-carrying half was measured directly: bundling `ui-slots/src` from
+  `HEAD` and from the patched tree, then registering
+  `{ name: 'test.list', id: 'mcp', order: 30, label: 'MCP', icon }`, yields
+  stored options `["id","order","label"]` on `HEAD` (the icon is dropped by the
+  option whitelist) and `["id","order","label","icon"]` on the patched tree.
+  That is the measured reason the interim installed-shell script is still
+  required on this release and why the Adapter does not yet pass `icon` at its
+  registration site.
